3. Performance
P2 — Establish a repeatable target-PC performance baseline — Measure frame pacing, startup, and memory with both exports and representative gameplay before optimizing; docs/PHASE_STATUS.md lists profiling as unverified, not a known current bottleneck.
P3 — Move idle-art validation work out of runtime setup — Precompute or store the visible-height scale used by _configure_idle_sprite() in game/scripts/combat/fighter_base.gd; this scans texture pixels at setup and may become unnecessary repeated work as the roster grows.
P3 — Pool transient effects only if profiling warrants it — Revisit pooling when hit sparks or other frequent spawned effects are added; the current code does not show a poolable VFX workload.
4. Code Quality
P2 — Split match orchestration into focused components — game/scripts/match/match_root.gd currently handles phase flow, hit resolution, pushbox separation, pause, and tie-breaking; separating those responsibilities would make later modes and regression tests easier to manage.
P2 — Separate fighter presentation data from combat control — game/scripts/combat/fighter_base.gd combines combat/state logic with character-specific art paths and clip playback; moving presentation lookup into data or dedicated presentation components would reduce coupling during roster expansion.
P2 — Make hitbox, hurtbox, and pushbox distinct — FighterBase.hurtbox_rect() currently returns pushbox_rect(); separate authored geometry would let combat hurt area and physical spacing be tuned independently.
P3 — Reconcile implementation-status documentation — Keep README.md, docs/KNOWN_ISSUES.md, docs/PHASE_STATUS.md, and docs/PIXELORAMA_PIPELINE.md aligned; some pipeline status text still describes older placeholder-animation status than the README and phase report.
